+# Cache Eviction Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is that the cache layer uses LRU (Least Recently Used) eviction, removing the least-recently-used entries when capacity is exceeded, with a fixed 300-second TTL applied to all cache entries. The rationale recorded for this decision is that LRU is simpler to reason about and predict than a frequency-based approach.
